          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A differential form is a geometrical object on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            that can be integrated. A differential form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/section"} section
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exterior+algebra"} exterior algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Λ
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda^* T^* X
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cotangent+bundle"} cotangent bundle
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+varieties"} algebraic varieties
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/analytic+space"} analytic spaces
          %p
            What we're actually describing here are the
            %em exterior
            differential forms; for more general concepts, see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+differential+form"} absolute differential form
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cogerm+differential+form"} cogerm differential form
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#standard_definition Standard definition
          %p
            Given a differentiable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "," do
